},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":566,"digest":"sha256:2b85ddc8baa9872117d26d2e47c13f611034168bf6b5e38baca4a284387e4bf5","download_count":209,"created_at":"2026-09-28T12:50:51Z","updated_at":"2026-09-28T12:50:51Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/releases/download/pcre2-10.49/pcre2-10.49.zip.sig"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PCRE2Project/pcre2/tarball/pcre2-10.49","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PCRE2Project/pcre2/zipball/pcre2-10.49","body":"This is a security-only release, to address [GHSA-r9hj-j2rw-4q3m](https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/security/advisories/GHSA-r9hj-j2rw-4q3m).\r\n\r\nCompared to 10.48, this release has only a minimal code change to prevent an out-of-bounds write with arbitrary data. An attacker-controlled regular expression is required. Applications are affected only when they use `pcre2_jit_stack_create()` and `pcre2_jit_stack_assign()` to provide a growable JIT stack, then match a pattern with unusually high JIT stack usage, such as one containing a large number of capturing groups.\r\n\r\nThe implications of an out-of-bounds write could include arbitrary code execution.\r\n\r\nThe issue is not a regression and affects releases 10.48 and earlier. Users should upgrade to 10.49. Backport patches for supported earlier releases are listed in [SUPPORT-LIFECYCLE.md](https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/blob/pcre2-10.49/SUPPORT-LIFECYCLE.md).\r\n\r\nThis release is available as a signed Git tag, or alternatively as a signed tarball of the Git tag ([attestation](https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/attestations/50757625)).","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/PCRE2Project/pcre2/releases/397384848/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1}}